# Claude
.claude/worktrees/**
# `claude mcp add --scope project` writes this file, and it holds the MCP
# server's env inline — including the Grafana service account token
# (docs/runbooks/grafana-query-access.md). Nothing else would catch it: the
# pre-commit hook and validation step 10 both only look at *secret*.yaml, so a
# token in JSON commits silently. Use the default local scope instead; this
# line is the backstop for when someone does not.
.mcp.json
# trivy-operator audit dumps (docs/runbooks/trivy-operator-audit.md). A snapshot
# of one cluster at one moment; a committed one would later read as current.
*-reports.json

# Byte-compiled sync.py (running its --self-check locally leaves these)
__pycache__/
